  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing communications to stakeholders, transparency and accountability at the Ministry of Finance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The project will support making the Ministry of Finance in Argentina more responsive to citizens and the private sector.  In order to do so, it will support the following activities: - Communications Audit at the Ministry of Finance. This needs assessment will establish strengths and weaknesses, defining a performance improvement plan based also in a benchmarking exercise with other G-20 Countries. -    Facilitation of the design and implementation of a results and performance based communications strategy- -   Generate a customized data base of external stakeholders at provincial/federal level -   Establish an online media center for Ministry of Finance and other ministries with up to the minute information to the media -   Develop a series of &quot;&quot;on the job training&quot;&quot; seminars for journalists, civil society, staff from Executive and Legislative powers on the impact of the economic crisis and the way forward -   Development of Interactive web based tools to communicate with the public and allow the processing of Access to Public Information requestspowers on the impact of the economic crisis and the way forward The overall objective of the proposed IDF grant is to improve the capacity of the Ministry of Finance in Argentina to deliver better and timely services  to the public and the media by increasing  transparency and accountability  Specific Objectives:  1. Strengthening the Ministry#s communications unit by identifying key institutional changes that need to be introduced and facilitating access to peer knowledge and good practices.  2. Supporting information request handling as well as pro-active transparency provisions at the Ministry, through the development of an ICT platform.  3. Supporting better understanding by the public of the activities performed by the Ministry of Finance, through enhancing services delivered to the media especially through its website and new media.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
